    "Is a 15-year mortgage better than a 30-year mortgage?": "¿Es mejor una hipoteca a 15 años que una a 30 años?",
    "A 15-year mortgage typically offers a lower interest rate and allows you to pay off your home twice as fast, saving you tens of thousands of dollars in interest. However, a 30-year mortgage has lower monthly payments, which provides greater cash flow flexibility and makes the home more affordable on a month-to-month basis.": "Una hipoteca a 15 años ofrece un tipo de interés más bajo y amortiza el inmueble el doble de rápido, ahorrando miles en intereses. Sin embargo, a 30 años la mensualidad es menor, ofreciendo mayor liquidez mes a mes.",
    "How do extra payments affect my mortgage payoff schedule?": "¿Cómo afectan los pagos adicionales al calendario de la hipoteca?",
    "Any extra money you pay towards your mortgage is applied directly to the principal balance. This reduces the remaining loan balance and decreases the amount of interest that accumulates, helping you pay off your mortgage years ahead of schedule and saving you a substantial amount in interest fees.": "Todo pago adicional amortiza directamente el capital principal. Esto reduce el saldo pendiente y los intereses futuros, permitiendo liquidar la hipoteca años antes y ahorrando gran cantidad de dinero.",
    "What is the Debt Snowball method?": "¿Qué es el método Bola de Nieve?",
    "The Debt Snowball method involves paying off your smallest debt balances first, regardless of interest rates. It builds psychological momentum and motivation through quick wins.": "El método Bola de Nieve consiste en liquidar primero las deudas de menor saldo, sin importar su tasa de interés. Proporciona impulso psicológico mediante victorias rápidas.",
    "What is the Debt Avalanche method?": "¿Qué es el método Avalancha?",
    "The Debt Avalanche method involves paying off your highest interest rate debts first. Mathematically, this minimizes the total interest you pay and helps you become debt-free faster.": "El método Avalancha liquida primero las deudas con la tasa de interés más alta. Matemáticamente minimiza el interés total pagado y acelera el fin de las deudas.",
    "Which method is better: Debt Snowball or Debt Avalanche?": "¿Cuál es mejor: Bola de Nieve o Avalancha?",
    "Mathematically, the Debt Avalanche method is superior because it minimizes the total interest paid. However, studies show that the Debt Snowball method is often more successful in practice because the psychological momentum of clearing individual accounts quickly helps people stay motivated and stick to their plan.": "Matemáticamente, la Avalancha es superior al minimizar intereses. Sin embargo, la Bola de Nieve suele tener mayor éxito práctico porque las victorias tempranas motivan a perseverar.",
    "How does the 'extra payment' roll over in these strategies?": "¿Cómo se transfiere el 'pago extra' en estas estrategias?",
    "In both methods, you continue paying the minimum required payments on all your debts. Any extra cash you can afford is added to the payment of your target debt (either the smallest balance or highest interest). Once that target debt is fully paid off, you roll its entire monthly payment (minimum + the extra cash) into the next debt on your list.": "En ambos métodos pagas el mínimo en todas las deudas y concentras el excedente en la deuda objetivo. Al liquidarla, transfieres todo ese monto mensual a la siguiente deuda.",
    "Can I do a hybrid of Snowball and Avalanche?": "¿Puedo hacer un híbrido entre Bola de Nieve y Avalancha?",
    "Yes. Some people prefer to pay off one or two small debts first to get immediate visual progress and free up cash flow (Snowball), and then pivot to targeting the remaining debts by highest interest rate to save on interest costs (Avalanche).": "Sí. Puedes pagar una o dos deudas pequeñas al principio para liberar flujo de caja (Bola de Nieve) y luego liquidar las restantes por tasa de interés más alta (Avalancha).",
    "When should I refinance my loan?": "¿Cuándo conviene refinanciar un préstamo?",
    "It generally makes sense to refinance if you can secure a lower interest rate, reduce your monthly payment, or shorten your term. The main goal is ensuring your total interest savings exceed the closing costs.": "Conviene refinanciar si obtienes una tasa menor, reduces la cuota o acortas el plazo, siempre que el ahorro en intereses supere los gastos de cierre.",
    "What closing costs are associated with refinancing?": "¿Qué costes de cierre conlleva la refinanciación?",
    "Refinancing costs typically include application fees, origination fees, appraisal costs, title search and insurance, credit report fees, and recording fees. These range from 2% to 6% of the loan amount.": "Incluyen costes de estudio, tasación, gestoría, registro y comisiones, que suelen oscilar entre el 2% y el 6% del importe solicitado.",
    "How do I calculate my refinance break-even point?": "¿Cómo calculo el punto de equilibrio de la refinanciación?",
    "To find your break-even point, divide your total refinance closing costs by your monthly payment savings. For example, if closing costs are $3,000 and you save $150 per month, your break-even point is 20 months ($3,000 / $150). If you plan to sell or move before reaching this point, refinancing may not make financial sense.": "Divide los costes totales de cierre entre el ahorro mensual obtenido. Por ejemplo, $3.000 de gastos / $150 de ahorro = 20 meses de amortización del gasto.",
    "What is the 28/36 rule?": "¿Qué es la regla 28/36?",
